{
  "about": "SAP Payment (10 Nov 2026): Manna Treads' incoming payments from customers, as SAP holds them, so the apps can list what a customer has paid and ERPNext can act when money arrives. Written only by B1iF's payments package through the Server Script manna_sap_payments (sap-b1if/erpnext): every customer payment posted in the current financial year, for customers ERPNext holds by custom_bp_code. A row is a mirror, never edited by hand. Named by sap_key = '<company>-<DocEntry>', as SAP Invoice is. A payment SAP cancels is kept and marked Cancelled, not deleted. Rows are inserted and saved as documents, so a Server Script on SAP Payment (After Insert / After Save) is the place for 'when a payment is received': act only when new_payment = 1, which a first load of old payments does not have.",
